IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc28-part26-extraordinary-remedies`

-- ccc28-tests-part26.l4 -- tests of sections 774 to 784. Expected values are written by hand from the words of each provision, on both sides of every threshold.

§ `s 774 and s 774.1`

#ASSERT `s 774 this Part applies to the proceedings` TRUE `s 774 certiorari` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 774 this Part applies to the proceedings` TRUE `s 774 habeas corpus` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 774 this Part applies to the proceedings` TRUE `s 774 mandamus` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 774 this Part applies to the proceedings` TRUE `s 774 procedendo` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 774 this Part applies to the proceedings` TRUE `s 774 prohibition` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 774 this Part applies to the proceedings` TRUE `s 774 another writ` EQUALS NOTHING   -- list not closed
#ASSERT `s 774 this Part applies to the proceedings` FALSE `s 774 certiorari` EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a criminal matter
#ASSERT `s 774.1 the person who is the subject of a writ of habeas corpus appears in court in person as they must` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 774.1 the person who is the subject of a writ of habeas corpus appears in court in person as they must` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 774.1 the person who is the subject of a writ of habeas corpus appears in court in person as they must` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#TRACE `s 774.1 the duty of the person who is the subject of a writ of habeas corpus to appear in person` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 774.1 the person who is the subject of a writ of habeas corpus` DOES `s 774.1 appear in court in person` AT 0

#TRACE `s 774.1 the duty of the person who is the subject of a writ of habeas corpus to appear in person` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 3)

§ `s 775: further detention on an inquiry`

#ASSERT `s 775 the judge or court may take this course without determining the question` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 775 make an order for the further detention of the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 775 the judge or court may take this course without determining the question` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 775 direct a judge, justice or provincial court judge to take proceedings, hear evidence or do another thing that will best further the ends of justice` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 775 the judge or court may take this course without determining the question` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `s 775 direct a judge, justice or provincial court judge to take proceedings, hear evidence or do another thing that will best further the ends of justice` EQUALS NOTHING   -- not in the opinion of the judge or court
#ASSERT `s 775 the judge or court may take this course without determining the question` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 775 a course the section does not name` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 775 the judge or court may take this course without determining the question` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 775 make an order for the further detention of the person` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- proceedings not instituted before a judge or court having jurisdiction
#ASSERT `s 775 the judge or court may take this course without determining the question` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE `s 775 make an order for the further detention of the person` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the person is not in custody by reason of a charge or a conviction
#ASSERT `s 775 the judge or court may take this course without determining the question` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `s 775 make an order for the further detention of the person` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not to have the legality of the imprisonment determined

§ `ss 776 to 778: conviction or order not reviewable, and remediable`

#ASSERT `s 776 the conviction or order shall not be removed by certiorari` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a) an appeal was taken
#ASSERT `s 776 the conviction or order shall not be removed by certiorari` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b) appeared, pleaded, merits tried, appeal might have been taken and was not
#ASSERT `s 776 the conviction or order shall not be removed by certiorari` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b) but the defendant did appeal: none of the "where" holds
#ASSERT `s 776 the conviction or order shall not be removed by certiorari` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the defendant did not appear and plead and the merits were not tried
#ASSERT `s 776 the conviction or order shall not be removed by certiorari` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no appeal might have been taken
#ASSERT `s 777(1) the conviction, order or warrant shall not be held to be invalid by reason of the irregularity, informality or insufficiency` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 777(1) the conviction, order or warrant shall not be held to be invalid by reason of the irregularity, informality or insufficiency` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- no punishment imposed: (c) "if any"
#ASSERT `s 777(1) the conviction, order or warrant shall not be held to be invalid by reason of the irregularity, informality or insufficiency` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (a) not satisfied
#ASSERT `s 777(1) the conviction, order or warrant shall not be held to be invalid by reason of the irregularity, informality or insufficiency` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b) not satisfied
#ASSERT `s 777(1) the conviction, order or warrant shall not be held to be invalid by reason of the irregularity, informality or insufficiency` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (c) not satisfied
#ASSERT `s 777(1) the conviction, order or warrant shall not be held to be invalid by reason of the irregularity, informality or insufficiency` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not removed by certiorari
#ASSERT `s 777(1) the conviction, order or warrant shall not be held to be invalid by reason of the irregularity, informality or insufficiency` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- invalidity on another ground
#ASSERT `s 777(1) the court or judge has the same powers to deal with the proceedings as a court to which an appeal might have been taken` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 777(1) the court or judge has the same powers to deal with the proceedings as a court to which an appeal might have been taken` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a conviction, order or warrant removed by certiorari
#ASSERT `s 777(2) the court or judge shall correct the sentence or remit the matter` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 777(2) the court or judge shall correct the sentence or remit the matter` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 777(2) the court or judge shall correct the sentence or remit the matter` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not satisfied that the person was properly convicted
#ASSERT `s 777(2) the court or judge shall correct the sentence or remit the matter` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the punishment is not greater than the lawful punishment
#ASSERT `s 777(2)(a) the corrected sentence is in accordance with this paragraph` `s 777(2)(a)(i) a fine` 1000 1000 `two years` `two years` `two years` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a fine at the maximum
#ASSERT `s 777(2)(a) the corrected sentence is in accordance with this paragraph` `s 777(2)(a)(i) a fine` 1001 1000 `two years` `two years` `two years` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a fine a dollar over the maximum
#ASSERT `s 777(2)(a) the corrected sentence is in accordance with this paragraph` `s 777(2)(a)(ii) imprisonment` 0 0 `two years` `five years` (`Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a term below the maximum, the person has served less than the maximum
#ASSERT `s 777(2)(a) the corrected sentence is in accordance with this paragraph` `s 777(2)(a)(ii) imprisonment` 0 0 `five years` `five years` (`Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a term at the maximum
#ASSERT `s 777(2)(a) the corrected sentence is in accordance with this paragraph` `s 777(2)(a)(ii) imprisonment` 0 0 (`Length of time` OF 5, 0, 1, FALSE) `five years` (`Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a term a day over the maximum
#ASSERT `s 777(2)(a) the corrected sentence is in accordance with this paragraph` `s 777(2)(a)(ii) imprisonment` 0 0 `two years` `five years` `five years` EQUALS NOTHING   -- the person has served a term equal to the maximum: (ii) states no correction
#ASSERT `s 777(2)(a) the corrected sentence is in accordance with this paragraph` `s 777(2)(a)(ii) imprisonment` 0 0 `two years` `five years` `ten years` EQUALS NOTHING   -- the person has served more than the maximum
#ASSERT `s 777(2)(a) the corrected sentence is in accordance with this paragraph` `s 777(2)(a)(ii) imprisonment` 0 0 `two years` `five years` (`Length of time` OF 4, 11, 30, FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- served four years eleven months and thirty days: less than five years
#ASSERT `s 777(2)(a) the corrected sentence is in accordance with this paragraph` `s 777(2)(a)(iii) a fine and imprisonment` 1000 1000 `two years` `five years` (`Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- both within their maxima
#ASSERT `s 777(2)(a) the corrected sentence is in accordance with this paragraph` `s 777(2)(a)(iii) a fine and imprisonment` 1001 1000 `two years` `five years` (`Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the fine is over the maximum: (iii) sends the fine to (i)
#ASSERT `s 777(2)(a) the corrected sentence is in accordance with this paragraph` `s 777(2)(a)(iii) a fine and imprisonment` 1000 1000 `ten years` `five years` (`Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the term is over
#ASSERT `s 777(2)(a) the corrected sentence is in accordance with this paragraph` `s 777(2)(a)(iii) a fine and imprisonment` 1000 1000 `two years` `five years` `five years` EQUALS NOTHING   -- (ii) states no correction for a person who has served the maximum
#ASSERT `s 777(2)(b) the punishment imposed on remittal is not greater than the punishment that may be lawfully imposed` 1000 1000 `five years` `five years` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 777(2)(b) the punishment imposed on remittal is not greater than the punishment that may be lawfully imposed` 1001 1000 `five years` `five years` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 777(2)(b) the punishment imposed on remittal is not greater than the punishment that may be lawfully imposed` 1000 1000 (`Length of time` OF 5, 0, 1, FALSE) `five years` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 777(3) the document shall be amended to conform to the adjudication as varied` TRUE `s 777(3) the conviction` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 777(3) the document shall be amended to conform to the adjudication as varied` TRUE `s 777(3) a warrant of committal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 777(3) the document shall be amended to conform to the adjudication as varied` TRUE `s 777(3) another document` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 777(3) the document shall be amended to conform to the adjudication as varied` FALSE `s 777(3) the conviction` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not varied
#ASSERT `s 777(4) the statement is sufficient for the purposes of the document` TRUE `s 777(4) an information` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 777(4) the statement is sufficient for the purposes of the document` TRUE `s 777(4) a summons` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 777(4) the statement is sufficient for the purposes of the document` TRUE `s 777(4) an order` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 777(4) the statement is sufficient for the purposes of the document` TRUE `s 777(4) a warrant` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 777(4) the statement is sufficient for the purposes of the document` TRUE `s 777(4) another document` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 777(4) the statement is sufficient for the purposes of the document` FALSE `s 777(4) an information` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 778 section 777 is deemed by this section to apply` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a) past tense
#ASSERT `s 778 section 777 is deemed by this section to apply` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b) punishment less than might lawfully have been imposed
#ASSERT `s 778 section 777 is deemed by this section to apply` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (c) an omission to negative circumstances
#ASSERT `s 778 section 777 is deemed by this section to apply` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- none of (a) to (c): this section does not deem it

§ `ss 779 to 783`

#ASSERT `s 779(1) the court may prescribe by general order that no motion to quash shall be heard unless the defendant gives security` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 779(1) the court may prescribe by general order that no motion to quash shall be heard unless the defendant gives security` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 779(1) the motion to quash may not be heard under the general order` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a recognizance with sureties: the "unless" is met
#ASSERT `s 779(1) the motion to quash may not be heard under the general order` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a deposit: the "unless" is met
#ASSERT `s 779(1) the motion to quash may not be heard under the general order` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- neither: the motion may not be heard
#ASSERT `s 779(1) the motion to quash may not be heard under the general order` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a recognizance, but not on the condition the subsection states
#ASSERT `s 779(1) the motion to quash may not be heard under the general order` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no general order prescribed
#ASSERT `s 779(2) the provisions of Part XXV relating to forfeiture of an amount set out in a recognizance apply` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 779(2) the provisions of Part XXV relating to forfeiture of an amount set out in a recognizance apply` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 780 the order refusing the application is sufficient authority for the clerk of the court to return the conviction, order or proceeding` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 780 the order refusing the application is sufficient authority for the clerk of the court to return the conviction, order or proceeding` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 781(1) the order, conviction or other proceeding shall not be quashed or set aside, nor the defendant discharged, by reason of this want of evidence` TRUE `s 781(1)(a) a proclamation or order of the Governor in Council or the lieutenant governor in council` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 781(1) the order, conviction or other proceeding shall not be quashed or set aside, nor the defendant discharged, by reason of this want of evidence` TRUE `s 781(1)(b) rules, regulations or by-laws made by the Governor in Council or the lieutenant governor in council` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 781(1) the order, conviction or other proceeding shall not be quashed or set aside, nor the defendant discharged, by reason of this want of evidence` TRUE `s 781(1)(c) the publication of a proclamation, order, rule, regulation or by-law in the Canada Gazette or in the official gazette for the province` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 781(1) the order, conviction or other proceeding shall not be quashed or set aside, nor the defendant discharged, by reason of this want of evidence` TRUE `s 781 another matter` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 781(1) the order, conviction or other proceeding shall not be quashed or set aside, nor the defendant discharged, by reason of this want of evidence` FALSE `s 781(1)(a) a proclamation or order of the Governor in Council or the lieutenant governor in council` EQUALS NOTHING   -- not by reason only of want of evidence
#ASSERT `s 781(2) the matter shall be judicially noticed` `s 781(1)(a) a proclamation or order of the Governor in Council or the lieutenant governor in council` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 781(2) the matter shall be judicially noticed` `s 781(1)(b) rules, regulations or by-laws made by the Governor in Council or the lieutenant governor in council` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 781(2) the matter shall be judicially noticed` `s 781(1)(c) the publication of a proclamation, order, rule, regulation or by-law in the Canada Gazette or in the official gazette for the province` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 781(2) the matter shall be judicially noticed` `s 781 another matter` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 782 the warrant of committal shall not be held to be void by reason of the defect` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 782 the warrant of committal shall not be held to be void by reason of the defect` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (a) not alleged in the warrant
#ASSERT `s 782 the warrant of committal shall not be held to be void by reason of the defect` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b) no valid conviction
#ASSERT `s 782 the warrant of committal shall not be held to be void by reason of the defect` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not on certiorari or habeas corpus
#ASSERT `s 782 the warrant of committal shall not be held to be void by reason of the defect` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not by reason only of a defect
#ASSERT `s 783 the court or judge may order that no civil proceedings shall be taken against the justice, provincial court judge or officer` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 783 the court or judge may order that no civil proceedings shall be taken against the justice, provincial court judge or officer` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not in quashing
#ASSERT `s 783 the court or judge may order that no civil proceedings shall be taken against the justice, provincial court judge or officer` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not an application of that kind
#ASSERT `s 783 the court or judge may order that no civil proceedings shall be taken against the justice, provincial court judge or officer` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not on the ground that he exceeded his jurisdiction

§ `s 784: appeals`

#ASSERT `s 784(1) an appeal lies to the court of appeal from the decision` `s 774 mandamus` `s 784(1) a decision granting the relief sought` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 784(1) an appeal lies to the court of appeal from the decision` `s 774 certiorari` `s 784(1) a decision refusing the relief sought` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 784(1) an appeal lies to the court of appeal from the decision` `s 774 prohibition` `s 784(1) a decision granting the relief sought` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 784(1) an appeal lies to the court of appeal from the decision` `s 774 prohibition` `s 784(1) another decision` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 784(1) an appeal lies to the court of appeal from the decision` `s 774 habeas corpus` `s 784(1) a decision granting the relief sought` EQUALS NOTHING   -- habeas corpus is not named in subsection (1)
#ASSERT `s 784(1) an appeal lies to the court of appeal from the decision` `s 774 procedendo` `s 784(1) a decision refusing the relief sought` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 784(2) Part XXI applies to the appeal` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 784(2) Part XXI applies to the appeal` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "Except as provided in this section"
#ASSERT `s 784(2) Part XXI applies to the appeal` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 784(3) no application may again be made on the same grounds` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 784(3) no application may again be made on the same grounds` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "unless fresh evidence is adduced"
#ASSERT `s 784(3) no application may again be made on the same grounds` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- other grounds: the bar is limited to the same grounds
#ASSERT `s 784(3) no application may again be made on the same grounds` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the application was not refused by a judge
#ASSERT `s 784(3) an appeal lies to the court of appeal from the refusal` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 784(3) an appeal lies to the court of appeal from the refusal` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 784(3) a further appeal lies to the Supreme Court of Canada` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 784(3) a further appeal lies to the Supreme Court of Canada` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- without leave: the subsection says the appeal lies "with leave"
#ASSERT `s 784(3) a further appeal lies to the Supreme Court of Canada` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the application was not refused on the appeal
#ASSERT `s 784(4) an appeal lies from the granting of the writ` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 784(4) an appeal lies from the granting of the writ` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 784(5) the appeal lies at the instance of this appellant` TRUE `s 784(5) an appeal to the court of appeal` `s 784(5) the applicant` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 784(5) the appeal lies at the instance of this appellant` TRUE `s 784(5) an appeal to the court of appeal` `s 784(5) the Attorney General of the province concerned` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 784(5) the appeal lies at the instance of this appellant` TRUE `s 784(5) an appeal to the court of appeal` `s 784(5) the Attorney General of Canada` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 784(5) the appeal lies at the instance of this appellant` TRUE `s 784(5) an appeal to the court of appeal` `s 784(5) any other party` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "but not at the instance of any other party"
#ASSERT `s 784(5) the appeal lies at the instance of this appellant` TRUE `s 784(5) an appeal from a judgment of the court of appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada` `s 784(5) the applicant` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 784(5) the appeal lies at the instance of this appellant` TRUE `s 784(5) an appeal from a judgment of the court of appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada` `s 784(5) the applicant` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- with leave of that Court
#ASSERT `s 784(5) the appeal lies at the instance of this appellant` TRUE `s 784(5) an appeal from a judgment of the court of appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada` `s 784(5) any other party` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 784(5) the appeal lies at the instance of this appellant` FALSE `s 784(5) an appeal to the court of appeal` `s 784(5) the applicant` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no judgment on the return of a writ
#ASSERT `s 784(6) the appeal is heard at an early date as it shall be` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 784(6) the appeal is heard at an early date as it shall be` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 784(6) the appeal is heard at an early date as it shall be` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#TRACE `s 784(6) the court's duty to hear the appeal in a habeas corpus matter at an early date` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 784(6) hear the appeal at an early date` AT 0
